- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/timeshift.html
- Summary (EN): Makes its input cook at a different time than the node itself. You can use it to reach earlier or later frames, or to fetch data from a specific absolute frame.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud fait cuire son entrée à un autre instant que lui-même, pour lire des images antérieures ou postérieures ou une frame absolue donnée.

- Inputs meaning: ["input1: the only input. The page gives no further description of its content."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Method", "meaning": "Whether the input is cooked at a frame number or at a time in seconds."}, {"name": "Mode", "meaning": "Absolute Shift moves an origin to a destination. Relative Shift applies an offset. Custom takes a value meant to be driven by an expression."}, {"name": "Frame / Time", "meaning": "The frame or time to pull (Custom), or the offset (Relative Shift)."}, {"name": "Shift from / to", "meaning": "The anchor and its new position (Absolute Shift)."}, {"name": "Integer Frames", "meaning": "Rounds frame numbers down to integers after the other calculations."}, {"name": "Clamp", "meaning": "Limits the retrieved value to the start, the end, both, or neither."}, {"name": "Start/End Frame or Time", "meaning": "Bounds used by Clamp. Shown only when Clamp is not None."}]

- Caveats: ["In Copernicus blocks, Time Shift cannot be used when block inputs must cook at different times. Suggested workaround: a Time Pack before Block Begin, with the frames wired in as a cable.", "For Relative Shift, a negative offset moves the input forward in time, the opposite of what the name suggests."]

